GPRIM-BYTEOFF: prim-node advances _gprim1/_gprim2 + N are BYTE strides

The rasterizer-setup functions advance the current prim-node pointers by the RECORD size
(_gprimX + 0x14 / 0x18 / ... = the 20/24-byte GPU primitive records, same stride family as
GPOLY-BYTEOFF patch 030), and Ghidra's undefined4* arithmetic prints raw byte addends. As
C int* the advance scaled x4, so every subsequent prim write landed 4x too far -- walking
out of the prim buffer straight through the adjacent ordering table (prim color words
0xa3a3/0x24af-links inside the OT, DrawOTag crash @0x24b6). Element uses (_gprim1[1],
*_gprim1) are 4-byte-correct and stay. Same byte-vs-element rule as patch 395 (_prim_buf).

